CORE
main.cob

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
cobol:division-by-zero
A zero divisor handled by an ON SIZE ERROR phrase is well defined: the
division-by-zero condition is folded into the size-error test, so no
division-by-zero check is emitted and verification succeeds. IBM LR "SIZE
ERROR phrases".
